From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:30:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aot: ELF modules and a manifest instead of the Mach-O
 loader's inputs; imports; JIT entry from the harness (T6)

elf_module.py turns an NSO into an ELF plus a manifest derived from it (segments, dynamic section, exports,
imports, relocations, every function entry including PLT stubs the unwind data omits), checks a manifest
against its ELF, relocates modules (RELATIVE, ABS64, GLOB_DAT, JUMP_SLOT), binds symbols to loaded modules,
then host functions, and runs them through aot_lift. Imports are guest addresses that run host functions.
Tests use synthetic modules with PLT/GOT, relocated pointer tables, init_array and weak symbols, equal to
Unicorn running the same image.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: replaces the Mach-O-only module inputs for the AArch64 -> x86_64 recompilation (NX2Linux); host/loader.c and the shader chain are untouched
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch feat/teo-t6-manifeste-elf)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
